      "media": "text",
      "title": "Hello Python 3.15, goodbye 3.10, and now I can use 3.11",
      "url": "https://simonwillison.net/2026/Oct/12/python-3-15/",
      "publishedAt": "2026-10-12T18:15:38.000Z",
      "snippet": " <p>Python 3.15 <a href=\"https://www.python.org/downloads/release/python-3150/\">is here</a>! Here's the essential <a href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.15/whatsnew/3.15.html\">What's new in Python 3.15</a> guide, this year curated by 3.14 and 3.15 release manager Hugo van Kemenade. As someone who builds open source software that works in every supported Python version, I get to say goodbye to Python 3.10 and start embracing features from Python 3.11.</p> <p>First, some highlights from Python 3.15.</",
      "enclosure": null
    },
